.TH "SAPI-WHEEL" "1" "2026-10-15" "sapi 1.0.0" "Salt API CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
sapi-wheel \- Execute a Salt Master wheel function (client=wheel or wheel_async)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sapi sapi wheel <function> [args...] [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute a Salt Master wheel function (client=wheel or wheel_async)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-async\fR
Run asynchronously via wheel_async
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-args\fR
Pass all arguments as raw strings
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR \fISTRING\fR
Path to custom CA certificate bundle PEM (env: SALT_API_CA_BUNDLE)
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fISTRING\fR
Path to config.toml (default: ~/.config/sapi/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-eauth\fR \fISTRING\fR
Salt external auth backend: pam, ldap, file, sharedsecret (env: SALT_API_EAUTH)
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR
Skip TLS certificate verification (env: SALT_API_INSECURE)
.TP
\fB\-\-mcp\fR
Start the integrated MCP server over stdio
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI color output
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fISTRING\fR
Output format: pretty, json, yaml, table (env: SALT_API_OUTPUT)
.TP
\fB\-\-password\fR \fISTRING\fR
Salt API password (env: SALT_API_PASSWORD)
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR \fISTRING\fR
Configuration profile name (env: SALT_API_PROFILE)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR
HTTP request timeout, e.g. 60s (env: SALT_API_TIMEOUT)
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fISTRING\fR
Explicit X\-Auth\-Token override (env: SALT_API_TOKEN)
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-url\fR \fISTRING\fR
Salt API base URL, e.g. https://salt:8000 (env: SALT_API_URL)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fISTRING\fR
Salt API username (env: SALT_API_USER)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
  sapi wheel key.list_all
  sapi wheel config.values
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsapi\fR(1)
